===Etymology===
From '''[[rag]]'''

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|verb form}} {{enPR|răgd}}, {{IPA|/ræɡd/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/r{gd/}}
* {{a|adjective}} {{enPR|răg'ĭd}}, {{IPA|/ˈræɡɪd/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"r{gId/}}

===Verb===
'''ragged'''

# {{en-past of|rag}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Rent or worn into tatters, or till the texture is broken.
#: ''a '''ragged''' coat''
#: ''a '''ragged''' sail''
# Broken with rough edges; having jags; uneven; rough; jagged.
#: '''''ragged''' rocks''
# Hence, harsh and disagreeable to the ear; [[dissonant]].
#* {{rfdate}} [[w:George Herbert|George Herbert]].
#*: A '''ragged''' noise of mirth.
# Wearing tattered clothes.
#: ''a '''ragged''' fellow''
# Rough; shaggy; rugged.
#* {{rfdate}}, [[w:John Dryden|John Dryden]].
#*: What shepherd owns those '''ragged''' sheep?
# {{rfdef|lang=en}}
#* {{quote-news
|year=2012
